<!--
  AbroBot CRM — crm.mnbresearch.com

  `/` IS LISTED NOW. It previously was not, and the note here said why: "the
  application at / and its routes are deliberately absent: they render as an
  empty React shell to a crawler and resolve to a login screen". Both halves of
  that have changed.

  `/` no longer resolves to a login screen — App.tsx renders the landing page
  there for signed-out visitors — and it no longer renders as an empty shell,
  because index.html now ships a real text hero inside <div id="root"> for
  clients that do not execute JavaScript. It also carries its own canonical,
  title, description, OG tags and structured data. So it is a real page, it is
  the page this product should be found by, and it belongs here.

  The app's OTHER routes are still absent, and still for the original reason.
  They are Disallow-ed in robots.txt; listing a disallowed URL in a sitemap is
  a direct contradiction — it asks a crawler to index something it has been
  told not to fetch, and Search Console reports it as an error.

  Extensionless URLs throughout. Cloudflare Pages normalises .html away, so
  /product is the address that answers 200 and /product.html 308-redirects to
  it — listing the .html form would advertise a redirect as a canonical.

  Priorities are relative, and only meaningful against each other. `/` takes
  the 1.0 that /product used to hold: it is the front door, it carries the
  live assistant, and it is where we want the brand query to land. /product
  keeps the long-form detail and stays just behind it.
-->
